    [CI][Docker] Specify flash-attention-npu build target for v0.32.0rc (#20557)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Apply the same `flash-attention-npu` build-target fix as #20556 to
    `releases/v0.32.0rc`.
    
    Set `FLASH_ATTN_BUILD_NPU=910` in the A2/A3 Ubuntu and openEuler
    Dockerfiles. The `2e532049` dependency pin added by #20523 defaults to
    automatic device detection, which fails on CPU-only Docker builders
    because no physical NPU is visible.
    
    Selecting the 910 backend explicitly compiles the correct A2/A3
    extensions without requiring NPU hardware during the image build.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No API or runtime behavior change. This fixes A2/A3 base-image builds
    for the v0.32.0rc release branch.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified the diff changes only the `flash-attention-npu` install
    command in the four A2/A3 Ubuntu and openEuler Dockerfiles.
    - Verified every affected build sets `FLASH_ATTN_BUILD_NPU=910`.
    - Full image builds were not run locally because the CANN/Ascend image
    build environment is provided by CI.
    - The A2/A3 Ubuntu and openEuler image matrix should be rerun for amd64
    and arm64.
    
